// Title: Fsutil Suspicious Invocation
// Sigma ID: add64136-62e5-48ea-807e-88638d02df1e
// Status: stable | Level: high
// Author: Ecco, E.M. Anhaus, oscd.community
// Date: 2019-09-26 | Modified: 2023-09-09
// ATT&CK: impact, stealth, T1070, T1485
// Description: Detects suspicious parameters of fsutil (deleting USN journal, configuring it with small size,
//   etc). Might be used by ransomwares during the attack (seen by NotPetya and others).
// False positives:
//   - Admin activity
//   - Scripts and administrative tools used in the monitored environment
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/fsutil-usn
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1070/T1070.md
//   - https://eqllib.readthedocs.io/en/latest/analytics/c91f422a-5214-4b17-8664-c5fcf115c0a2.html
//   - https://github.com/albertzsigovits/malware-notes/blob/558898932c1579ff589290092a2c8febefc3a4c9/Ransomware/Lockbit.md
//   - https://blog.cluster25.duskrise.com/2023/05/22/back-in-black-blackbyte-nt
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_fsutil_usage.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\fsutil.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "fsutil.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "deletejournal" or ProcessCommandLine contains "createjournal" or ProcessCommandLine contains "setZeroData")
